5,1,1,talk,Daisuke,,I... I think we should look at the things that happen every day. I will check the misrouted deliveries in the incident logs and the time lost to copying existing records.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,May,,"I'll keep things interesting! I want to see who's actually doing the work, so I'll check the staffing of the coordination group and the in-house developer availability.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,Shunichi,,I'll handle the external variables. I will examine the network coverage at customer plants and the handling of vendor queries. Let's see if our assumptions actually match reality.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Ryuji,,"I will examine the capital budget and software allowance, as well as the vendor licence pricing versus fixed-fee work. We must be clear on the financial commitments.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Kenji,,I want to see if we're actually learning from the past! I'll check the outcomes of the last three internal rollouts and the record of cross-unit standardization efforts. Let's find a real winner!,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
