25,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"It seems... we are losing a lot of time. People are spending nearly an hour every day just copying records that already exist, and we have several misrouted deliveries because of inconsistent addresses.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,May,,"Oh, it's even more chaotic than I thought! Our coordination group is basically a ghost town, yet two poor souls are still doing everything by hand. It's practically a miracle anything gets done.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"It's almost poetic. We're operating on a fantasy. Half the customer plants have dead zones for entire afternoons, and getting a device approved takes six weeks. Our ""seamless"" integration is a myth.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The financial situation is precarious. The capital budget is frozen, meaning we cannot afford new hardware or major infrastructure. However, we have some room in the recurring software allowance due to recent write-offs.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"I've found a pattern! The big, fancy projects that require everyone to participate just fade away. But the small, specific tools for one trade—and the tool room walkthroughs—are actually still being used!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@May, it sounds like those two people are really struggling. If we keep ignoring the small, daily errors, they'll just keep burning out.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,May,,"Exactly, Daisuke! We treat staff time like it's a magic, infinite resource. If we pick a project that adds more ""manual coordination"" to their plate, we're just asking for a total collapse.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, if the budget is frozen for hardware, we can't afford to ignore the fact that our connectivity at customer sites is a disaster. Any plan relying on real-time remote access is a daydream.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, I agree. We must avoid any proposal requiring new hardware or site-wide infrastructure. We should focus on software solutions that fit within our existing recurring allowance to avoid future budget shocks.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Ryuji, that makes sense! But we also have to make sure the software is actually useful. If it's too big and complicated, people will just stop using it like they did before!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I agree with Kenji. If we choose something too complex, it might just make the daily work harder. Maybe we should look for something that simply stops the waste of time and the mistakes.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,3,talk,May,,"@Kenji, you're spot on. We need something lean. And let's be real—if the project requires our in-house developers, we're stuck. They're tied up until the third quarter, and the documentation is a mess.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, so we have no developers and no signal at the plants. It's a wonder we're even discussing ""innovation."" We need a project that doesn't require a miracle to deploy or a developer to maintain.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, precisely. Furthermore, we must be wary of per-head licensing. If a tool's cost scales with every department we add, it will create a financial burden that we cannot sustain once the initial fund is spent.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Ryuji, that's a great point! We should look for something that's a ""small win""—a tool that helps a specific group without needing a huge budget or everyone's constant attention to survive. Let's keep it simple!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I hope we can find something that helps the people on the floor. If we can just stop the copying and the address errors, it would mean so much to them.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
41,2,4,pass,Daisuke,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
42,2,4,talk,May,,"I'm with you, Daisuke. Let's find something that actually lightens the load instead of just adding another ""innovation"" for the exhausted staff to manage. I'm ready to see the candidates!","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
43,2,4,pass,May,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
44,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"I'm quite looking forward to this. Let's see if any of the candidates are grounded in reality, or if they're just more expensive fantasies for us to manage. I'm ready.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
45,2,4,pass,Shunichi,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
46,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,I agree. We need a solution that is fiscally sustainable and operationally lean. I am ready to evaluate the candidates based on these constraints.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
47,2,4,pass,Ryuji,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
48,2,4,talk,Kenji,,I'm super excited too! Let's find a project that's actually going to stick and make people's lives easier. I'm ready!,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
