55,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think Candidate C, the Supplier Data Hub, is the best. It could stop the address errors and the time wasted copying records. It seems like it would really help the people struggling.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,May,,"C is tempting, but @Daisuke, who actually maintains that ""shared update procedure""? If it's just more manual work for our ghost-town coordination group, it's a trap. I'm leaning toward D for now.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"D is just a fancy way to automate meeting notes, which is hardly ""innovation."" As for A, it's a disaster waiting to happen. Our customer plant connectivity is a joke; a mobile app is a daydream.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Candidate A is indeed a risk given the network dead zones Shunichi mentioned. Candidate B requires a production unit, which likely involves capital expenditure for hardware that we cannot afford. I lean toward Candidate C.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"I'm with Daisuke and Ryuji! Candidate C is a specific tool for a specific need. My research shows that narrow tools for one trade actually survive, while big, shared things like Candidate D usually just fade away!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Daisuke"",""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@May, I... I think the hub would be better than more manual work. If the records are in one place, the people in the depot wouldn't have to copy them by hand anymore. It would save them so much time.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, I want to believe that, but ""shared procedures"" usually mean someone is stuck doing the data entry. If we don't have developers to automate it, it's just a new chore for the same exhausted people.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, you're actually being rational for once. But look at the alternative: Candidate C is a central repository. It doesn't require a signal at a customer plant or a production studio. It's the only one that isn't a total fantasy.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@May, if we prioritize a fixed-fee build for the hub, we avoid the per-head licensing costs that would make a tool like Candidate D a long-term liability. It is the most fiscally responsible choice.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@May, think about the tool room walkthroughs I found! They were simple and specific, and people still want them. Candidate C is like that—it's a practical resource, not a complicated system that needs everyone's constant attention!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think we can make it work. If it stops the mistakes and the copying, the people on the floor will be so much happier. I really believe Candidate C is the kindest choice for them.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,May,,"@Ryuji, if you can guarantee a fixed-fee build that doesn't require our missing developers to maintain it, I'm in. I just can't support anything that treats our staff's sanity as a free resource. C it is!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"It seems we've finally reached a consensus. Candidate C is the only option that doesn't rely on a miracle of connectivity or a budget that doesn't exist. It's a boring, practical choice—which is exactly why it's the right one.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,I concur. Candidate C addresses the operational waste Daisuke identified while remaining within our software allowance and avoiding the capital freeze. It is the only proposal that is both logically sound and financially sustainable.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"This is awesome! We all agree! Candidate C is the perfect ""small win"" that actually helps people without being a giant, failing project. I'm voting for the Supplier Data Hub!","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,I... I'm very glad we could agree on this. I'll vote for Candidate C. I really hope it makes things easier for everyone.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,4,talk,May,,"I'm sold! As long as we aren't just handing a bigger shovel to the same two exhausted people, I'm all for it. My vote goes to Candidate C!","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,I'll join the party. It's the only choice that doesn't require us to pretend our infrastructure actually works. My vote is for Candidate C.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,"My vote is for Candidate C. It is the most rational selection, ensuring we avoid capital expenditure and unsustainable licensing costs while solving a tangible operational problem.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,4,talk,Kenji,,I'm voting for Candidate C too! It's the most reliable way to actually help our teammates and make sure the project lasts. Let's do this!,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
